      armored enemy is built from the thug''s branches with a different roster. It
      holds its place on the ring like a wall where a thug prowls (HoldSlot, not
      Prowl), and it never taunts. Its armor is not in the tree at all: it is its
      hit receiver profile, which shrugs off a jab and turns a stagger into a flinch
      until the enemy is stunned.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"49b617c6-d2d9-4ccf-8899-bab66a11bd11","$type":"ArcaneOnyx.GraphCore.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3700.0,"yMin":-260.0,"xMax":-3400.0,"yMax":-110.0},"title":"Entered,
      never taken over","body":"The guard of Attack checks only at the door, on purpose:
      a swing that started plays to its end unless a reaction above cuts it short.
      bt_verify reports it for that reason.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"984197e8-eae3-46ca-8a94-04e60f6821eb","$type":"ArcaneOnyx.GraphCore.StickyNote"},{"$ref":"12"},{"$ref":"17"},{"$ref":"21"},{"$ref":"25"},{"ScriptGraphVariable":{"returnType":"System.Object,
